abstract: >-
  A prospectively registered linear scalar-to-stress calibration on prescribed
  de Sitter geometry at the fixed minimal Euclidean/BD reference. Direct mode
  density and pressure are compared with independently integrated matched
  formulas, complete fixed-reference W2/W4 subtraction and local contacts.
  The package retains raw extended-precision modes, separate Ward ledgers,
  finite-cutoff trace terms, constructive omitted-momentum bounds and explicit
  numerical controls. This is a component calibration; no thermalization,
  quantum stability, coupled shell evolution or Big-Bang origin is established.
  Internal AI-assisted reviews are not external peer review.
